  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Just for the sake of consistency, it would be nice if we had the option to turn on a setting called \"Natural Vive hand gestures\"\n\nMy ideas for each hand gesture (basically a direct port of the documented hand gesture controls from the oculus touch translated to the vive wands)\n\nHand Open - Do nothing\nVictory - Thumb on trackpad \nFinger Point - Hold grip while thumb is on touchpad\nHandgun - Hold grip button\nThumbs up - Hold trigger and grip button\nFist - Thumb on touchpad, hold grip, trigger determines closed amount\nRock N Roll - Hold Trackpad, press trigger.\nNo gesture - Hold trigger down \n\nPS: I am aware some people will hate the idea of holding down the grip button, but I personally don't see why it's a problem, I can hold that sucker down for a few minutes without feeling anything, and doing hand gestures takes like 5 seconds, not to mention it is incredibly confusing doing it with the trackpad, also keep in mind I'm proposing a MENU OPTION, not a complete replacement of the gesture system...",
